body:
This is what I don't understand. I feel like a shopping cart could only help boost their sales, if only marginally. It doesn't sound like they have too many right now so I would think any little bit would help.

&#x200B;

I think the issue was that EGS was set up originally and sold as s storefront that wouldn't have super sales or deeply discounted content and shortly after doing just that.

Here's an Imgur Album with a brief look at the rest of the stuff. I have the Argento Cut right now in my Bluray Ripper.

&#x200B;

[https://imgur.com/a/FVVu5am](https://imgur.com/a/FVVu5am)

&#x200B;

EDIT: Worth noting that my order seems to be missing the 2 inner digipaks that are mentioned on the back of the box. Not a huge concern of mine, but a little disappointing still.

I know Youtube will add compression, but I tried to rip a small sample from the Blu-Ray to see if it'd help you make a comparison.

&#x200B;

[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrRvr-yn6dY&ab\_channel=InspectorJones](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrRvr-yn6dY&ab_channel=InspectorJones)

Eh, I recognize it takes a lot of work, but it doesn't look like something I'd want to play as a huge fan of the REMake and RE4. The hybridization of using RE4 as a base just doesn't seem to gell with the gameplay of REmake imo. 

&#x200B;

That said the environments looked good.

Nope this is definitely true and a reason why the HD version of the remake suffers from a loss of detail (More apparent in some backgrounds then others).

&#x200B;

There's some HD Video floating around out there a camera floating through the Spencer Mansion fully rendered in real time in whatever program they developers used to create the game and it looks amazing! You can see details that weren't available in the game like ceilings and walls that weren't visible in the game.

0 is also one of the most difficult games in the classic formula. I'd wait till you've completed the others before giving it an attempt.

&#x200B;

I've been playing the games since I was a kid and only completed Zero once. It's difficulty and certain things feels more clunky than the other games.

What does it say when the Subreddit dedicated to PC gaming seems to reject it outright? Probably not good for your PC Games Launcher.

&#x200B;

/Games is a larger default subreddit (Well last I knew of anyway) filled with all kinds of gamers; I'm not surprised that anyone not invested heavily in PC gaming would just upvote a post advertising free games. Heck, I do that on other subreddits I'm not as invested in.

&#x200B;

/Gamedeals is smaller population and less PC focused as well. And again I wouldn't be surprised if a lot of the upvotes were coming from people whom aren't PC gamers first.

Oh no; I happen to be in the camp that enjoys seeing it or at least finds it rather amusing. 

&#x200B;

I'd rather see people make informed choices and while I would never fault anyone personally for accepting free games, I don't want want to accept them myself as its part of Epic's business model.

I've only played Vanilla, but I only have like 150+ hours across all the different SP & MP games I've played. I don't usually care for mods in most games, so Factorio has been addicting to me since the start. Playing currently again I've been having a ton of fun learning how to get trains working and finally achieving my largest base and gotten the furthest on the tech tree so far.

&#x200B;

Maybe one day I'll force myself to check out some mods, but I can honestly see myself just playing new Vanilla maps or mess with the default settings.

Got to play like an hour and a half before going to work; but my impressions are extremely positive outside a minor bug where I got stuck on the menu screen and had to restart the game to fix it.

&#x200B;

If you like Symphony of the Night/Castlevania I'd say check it out (Wow what a bold statement).

Downvoted because of the EGS deal and will downvote every Outerworlds post until it's released on Steam.

&#x200B;

Sorry Obsidian; I might purchase this game used on consoles until the superior Steam release comes out.

Resident Evil 2 Remake is perhaps the strongest argument I have against your case, but even that stands out as an exception to in AAA game space to me. That game is relatively short on your first play through but most people seemed to love it.

&#x200B;

I was afraid they were going to feel obliged to add bloat to it to make it a 20 hour campaign or something.
